    "text": "To determine how much Gina will spend in total, we need to calculate the cost of her credits, textbooks, and facilities fee separately, and then sum these amounts.\n\n1. **Calculate the cost of the credits:**\n   Gina is taking 14 credits, and each credit costs $450.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of credits} = 14 \\times 450 = 6300\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the cost of the textbooks:**\n   Gina has to pay $120 for each of her 5 textbooks.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of textbooks} = 5 \\times 120 = 600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the facilities fee:**\n   The facilities fee is a flat rate of $200.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Facilities fee} = 200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   Add the cost of the credits, the cost of the textbooks, and the facilities fee.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = 6300 + 600 + 200 = 7100\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount Gina will spend is \\(\\boxed{7100}\\).",
